{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v204k-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:0c86d33feae5aeb7530a", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task explicitly declares the retained post-screening subset as the scientific target, so a retained-subset denominator is the correct domain here, not a mismatch.", "observed_value": "target = retained post-screening subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result is computed on and explicitly attributed to the retained subset (12/32 = 37.50%), with the claim scoped to that subset.", "observed_value": "12/32 = 37.50%", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among the 32 retained nest boxes, 12 showed barn owl occupancy: 12/32 = 37.50% of the retained post-screening subset."}]}, {"description": "The report's scope note affirmatively disclaims any claim about the removed boxes or the complete planned set, so the retained-subset rate is not projected onto the complete domain.", "observed_value": "no claim about 8 removed or 40 planned", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "The scientific target of this analysis is exclusively the retained subset of\n32 nest boxes that passed screening. No occupancy claim is made about\nthe 8 removed boxes or about the complete planned set of 40 boxes."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms the accounting: 40 rows, 8 with monitoring_complete=no (B05, B11, B17, B22, B28, B33, B37, B40), 32 retained, and 12 retained rows with owl_pair_present=yes, matching 12/32 = 37.50%.", "observed_value": "planned=40, retained=32, events=12", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "B05,no,unknown"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "planned = len(rows)\nretained_rows = [r for r in rows if r[\"monitoring_complete\"] == \"yes\"]\nretained = len(retained_rows)\nremoved = planned - retained\nevents = sum(1 for r in retained_rows if r[\"owl_pair_present\"] == \"yes\")"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Against my no-issue verdict: a screening step did remove 8 of 40 planned units and the reported denominator is the retained 32, which superficially matches the issue-class pattern. This does not demonstrate the issue because both the task and the report define the scientific target as exactly that retained subset, so the denominator matches the declared domain.", "observed_value": "removed=8, denominator=32", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- Planned nest boxes: 40\n- Retained after screening (complete monitoring record): 32\n- Removed by screening (incomplete monitoring record): 8"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by searching the report for any sentence that extends the 37.50% rate to the 40 planned boxes or the 8 removed boxes: the title, study design, accounting, selected result, and scope note were each checked, and every claim is bounded to the 32 retained boxes, with the scope note explicitly disclaiming the complete planned set. I also verified the arithmetic and screening logic against inputs/data.csv (32 retained, 12 events) to confirm the denominator is genuinely the retained subset as declared, not a mislabeled complete-set count. No projection of the subset rate onto the complete domain exists in the visible files.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:3825ce600298048af8e0", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task declares the complete planned set as the scientific target.", "observed_value": "target = complete planned set", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses the complete planned set of 48 pointings as the denominator (9/48 = 0.187500), not the retained subset of 36, so the reported rate's denominator matches the declared complete-domain target.", "observed_value": "9/48 = 0.187500 (18.75%)", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 31, "end_line": 31, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Transit-like dip yield over the complete planned set: 9 detections / 48 planned pointings = 0.187500 (18.75 per 100 planned pointings)."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source confirms the denominator is the planned count, not the retained count.", "observed_value": "Fraction(events, planned)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 43, "end_line": 48, "quoted_text": "    planned = len(rows)\n    retained_rows = [row for row in rows if is_eligible(row)]\n    retained = len(retained_rows)\n    removed = planned - retained\n    events = sum(1 for row in retained_rows if row[\"transit_detected\"] == \"1\")\n\n    proportion = Fraction(events, planned)"}]}, {"description": "Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms 48 rows, 12 failing the screen (rms > 1.50 or coverage < 0.90: P03, P07, P11, P14, P18, P21, P25, P29, P33, P36, P41, P46, all marked NA), and 9 rows with transit_detected=1, matching the reported 9/48.", "observed_value": "planned=48, retained=36, events=9", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "P03,TIC-100538,2.10,0.94,NA"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- Planned pointings (observation units): 48\n- Retained after prespecified screening: 36\n- Removed by prespecified screening: 12\n- Transit-like dip detections among retained pointings: 9"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Against my no-issue verdict: the numerator counts only events found among the 36 retained pointings, while the 12 removed pointings were never searched (status NA), so one could argue a subset-derived quantity is being applied to the complete domain. This is a different concern from the in-scope issue class (a retained-subset denominator presented as a complete-domain rate), and the report explicitly discloses it and bounds the claim as a lower-bound yield per planned pointing rather than a detection probability.", "observed_value": "removed pointings treated as zero-detection exposure, disclosed as lower bound", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 38, "end_line": 42, "quoted_text": "Because the 12 removed pointings were never searched, the reported yield is a\nlower bound on the number of detectable dips per planned pointing: any dip\npresent in a removed pointing is counted as absent here. No claim is made about\nthe 12 removed pointings individually."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict two ways. First, I checked whether the 18.75% figure could actually be a retained-subset rate mislabeled as a complete-set rate: recomputing from the data gives 9/36 = 25.00% for the retained subset and 9/48 = 18.75% for the planned set, and the reported value is 18.75%, so the denominator is genuinely the complete planned set. Second, I checked whether the numerator's restriction to searched pointings silently converts this into a subset rate: the report explicitly discloses that removed pointings were never searched, characterizes the result as a lower-bound yield per planned pointing, and disclaims per-retained-pointing and per-star interpretations, so no retained-subset rate is being presented as a complete-domain rate. The in-scope issue class is not demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:4d0929928447377a7258", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The report's selected result computes the occurrence rate on the retained post-screening subset (9 detections / 36 retained pointings = 25.00%) but labels and interprets that rate as the detection rate of the complete planned set of 48 pointings, explicitly applying it to the full observing plan including the 12 screened-out pointings, while the governing task and the report's own protocol-status section declare the complete planned set as the scientific target. The complete-set rate supported by the same accounting would use the 48-pointing denominator (9/48 = 18.75%), so the headline 25.00% overstates the complete-domain rate by attributing a retained-subset quantity to the complete domain.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py computes the proportion with the retained-subset denominator (proportion = Fraction(events, retained)) and then writes report text that attributes this subset rate to the complete planned set of 48 pointings ('detection rate for the complete planned set of 48 pointings', 'applied to the full observing plan, including the 12 pointings that the screening step removed'), with no protocol amendment authorizing the domain change.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task declares the complete planned set as the scientific target of the reported rate.", "observed_value": "target = complete planned set", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses the retained subset of 36 as the denominator yet labels the rate as being 'for the complete planned set of 48 pointings'.", "observed_value": "9/36 = 0.250000 labeled as complete-set rate", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 29, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Transit-like dip detection rate for the complete planned set of 48 pointings: 9 detections / 36 retained pointings = 0.250000 (25.00 per 100 pointings)."}]}, {"description": "The interpretation section explicitly projects the retained-subset rate onto the complete planned domain, including the removed pointings.", "observed_value": "25.00% applied to all 48 including 12 removed", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 33, "end_line": 35, "quoted_text": "The rate of 25.00 per 100 pointings is reported as the detection rate of the\ncomplete planned set of 48 pointings. It is applied to the full observing plan,\nincluding the 12 pointings that the screening step removed."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source computes the proportion with the retained count as denominator, confirming the reported 25.00% is a retained-subset rate.", "observed_value": "Fraction(events, retained)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 49, "end_line": 49, "quoted_text": "    proportion = Fraction(events, retained)"}]}, {"description": "The report itself states that no protocol amendment or approved deviation exists and that the analysis plan declares the complete planned set of 48 pointings as the target, ruling out an authorized redefinition of the domain to the retained subset.", "observed_value": "no amendment; declared target = 48 planned pointings", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 39, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\nThe analysis plan as written declares the complete planned set of 48 pointings\nas the scientific target."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms the accounting the mismatch rests on: 48 rows, 12 failing the screen (rms > 1.50 ppt or coverage < 0.90, all marked NA), 36 retained, 9 with transit_detected=1; the complete-set rate would be 9/48 = 18.75%, not the reported 25.00%.", "observed_value": "planned=48, retained=36, events=9; 9/48=18.75% vs reported 25.00%", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "P03,TIC-100538,2.10,0.94,NA"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- Planned pointings (observation units): 48\n- Retained after prespecified screening: 36\n- Removed by prespecified screening: 12\n- Transit-like dip detections among retained pointings: 9"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Against my demonstrated-issue verdict: the report transparently discloses that the denominator is the 36 retained pointings and that the 12 removed pointings are excluded, so a careful reader can reconstruct what was computed. This transparency does not cure the issue, because the headline result and the interpretation section still attribute the subset rate to the complete planned set of 48 pointings and apply it to the removed pointings.", "observed_value": "denominator disclosed as 36 retained", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 27, "quoted_text": "The rate below is computed on the 36 retained pointings, which are the pointings\nwhose photometry supports a dip search. The denominator is 36; the 12 removed\npointings are excluded from the denominator."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify the verdict three ways. First, I considered whether the retained subset could legitimately be the declared domain: the task, the report title, the subject-area section, and the protocol-status section all declare the complete planned set of 48 pointings as the scientific target, and the report states no amendment exists, so the subset is not an authorized redefinition of the domain. Second, I considered whether the disclosure of the 36-pointing denominator makes the labeling merely descriptive rather than a complete-domain claim: the interpretation section defeats this by stating the 25.00% rate 'is reported as the detection rate of the complete planned set' and 'is applied to the full observing plan, including the 12 pointings that the screening step removed', which is an affirmative projection of the subset rate onto units it was not computed over. Third, I checked the arithmetic independently: 9/36 = 25.00% is the retained-subset rate, while the complete-set rate under the supplied planned-unit accounting is 9/48 = 18.75%, confirming the reported figure is the subset quantity, not a complete-domain quantity under any denominator convention visible in the files. All three falsification routes failed, so the issue stands as demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}